<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<jmeterTestPlan version="1.2" properties="5.0" jmeter="5.6.3">
  <hashTree>
    <TestPlan guiclass="TestPlanGui" testclass="TestPlan" testname="23120274 - Load - Category Management &amp; Verification" enabled="true">
      <stringProp name="TestPlan.comments">[DE THIET KE, CHUA CHAY] Created 2026-11-18 (Asia/Saigon). Pool A+C; five HTTP requests/iteration.
Observed hardware 2026-11-18 16:05:55 +07:00: Intel i5-11400H, 6 cores/12 logical CPUs; RAM 15.74 GiB, free 1.65 GiB; Windows 11 Home 64-bit; disk E free 55.4 GiB.
Default proposal: 10 VU, ramp 20s, total main-group lifetime 180s (includes ramp), think 1000-2000ms ONCE before Login each iteration. No delay between Create/Delete. This is not a measured capacity or SLA. Reclaim memory before execution; preflight and iteration gates require &gt;=2048MiB free RAM inside the running JVM environment. Below the floor, no new iterations are permitted; pending records remain subject to guarded recovery.
DO NOT RUN before workload, isolation, credentials, baseline, stop conditions and recovery are reviewed. Mutation gates default false: hw05.allow_mutation and hw05.isolated_sut must explicitly be true after approval.
Properties: csv_file (default ../data/categories.csv relative to active JMX); project_root (default parent of test-plans); host=localhost, port=3000, protocol=http; load_threads=10 (allowed 1..20), ramp_seconds=20 (&gt;=threads), duration_seconds=180 (&gt;ramp); think_min_ms=1000, think_range_ms=1000; connect_timeout_ms=3000, response_timeout_ms=10000; run_id optional new namespace, engine_id=local, min_free_mib&gt;=2048.
Credentials exclusively ESHOP_ADMIN_EMAIL/ESHOP_ADMIN_PASSWORD. Never put their values in CLI/JMX/CSV. No exp requirement on SUT token. All token/ID/owner variables thread-local. CSV approved SHA256 c237523a3f44a5d1471b3d4483bcb25c76495e9972e6a0f2b6bf9bec0dc1a23e.
Setup captures real baseline/account state/config+source hashes when actually run; it performs extra preflight requests OUTSIDE the main measurement. Main JSR223 control samples and setup/teardown samples use setIgnore; there is no parent Transaction sample. Summary Report contains only main HTTP samples. No listener filename is configured; no JTL is generated by this design task.
Durable append-only per-thread manifest is forced to storage BEFORE Create is eligible; confirmed ID is persisted before Delete. Event stepName is separate from categoryName. Failed Login/View/Create skips dependent requests; continue-on-error preserves cleanup opportunities. Any contract/manifest failure stops NEW iterations/intents, while already-confirmed owned records may finish cleanup.
No extra guard GET/read-after-create in the five-request main workflow. Delete guard uses this iteration's durable intent + real Create ID, baseline/ref-ID exclusion and previously verified SUT contract. REQUIRES isolated SUT/no external product links/no backend restart; it is NOT atomic proof of current DB name/reference. Extra GET guards run in out-of-window recovery only. Create existence must be reconfirmed in an approved pilot; HTTP 200/Create message alone is not read-after-write proof.
Scheduler/graceful shutdown may leave a partial iteration. tearDown attempts exact-name guarded recovery plus full baseline/products/admin verification, but forced kill can skip it. Independent scripts/recover-category-load.groovy supports offline manifest preview; --apply additionally requires --quiescent and --isolated and fresh environment credentials. It locks the run, validates source/config/baseline, refuses ambiguous IDs/names or product references, then deletes exact owned rows only. Never reset database, restart SUT or delete by prefix.
Unknown Create outcome with no observed row remains RECOVERY_REQUIRED in automatic teardown: finite polling cannot rule out late writes. Independent recovery requires user confirmation of quiescence. Torn manifest lines or ownership mismatches fail closed. Active lock prevents recovery while this JVM run is active, but cannot prove that the server has finished every timed-out request.
Performance status and cleanup status are separate. JSON/helper compilation and JMX deserialization are static checks only. Pilot, timeout/forced-stop paths, real multi-thread behavior and resource limits remain unverified. Do not claim performance PASS without actual JTL/resource evidence. Disable debug HTTP logging and never save request/response bodies/headers; assertions scrub sample data before listeners.
</stringProp>
